Q: Multiple search-and-replace inside the same text A: <p><strong><em>Updated - Speed tests added at the end.</em></strong><br />
These tests are inconclusive as to which way is better, but note that it can't be<br />
done by starting over at the beginning of the target each time,<br />
in a while loop. This is many times (if not thousands of times) slower.<br />
And with a very large data set, time to get some coffee.</p>
<p>It could be done using the best of both worlds where
there is a loop around the substitution regex that starts anew
after/from the last recorded match (see regex comments how this is calculated).</p>
<p>This encompasses @BhuvaneswariBalan and @ikegami methods.
It is really a single pass regex leveraging <em><code>pos()</code></em> and the <em><code>\G</code></em> anchor,<br />
in a while loop and non-global.</p>
<p>This is a Single pass regex, Perl code demo  <a href="https://www.jdoodle.com/ia/1RAK" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://www.jdoodle.com/ia/1RAK</a> :</p>
<pre><code>use strict;
use warnings;

my $cp = 0; 

my $inp = &quot;text regtext1 text regtext2 text regtextA regtextZ end&quot;;
my $imod = $inp;

while ( $imod =~ s/\G.*?\K(reg)(text\d+(?{$cp=pos()}).*?)(regtext[A-Z]+)(?{$cp+=length($^N)})/$1$3$2/s ) {
    pos($imod) = $cp;
}

print ( &quot;\n$inp\n&quot;, $imod, &quot;\n&quot; );
</code></pre>
<p>Output:</p>
<pre><code>text regtext1 text regtext2 text regtextA regtextZ end
text regregtextAtext1 text regregtextZtext2 text   end
</code></pre>
<hr />
<p><em><strong>Speed tests</strong></em> :<br />
These two methods are the only really viable ways.</p>
<pre><code>use strict;
use warnings;
use Benchmark ':hireswallclock';

my $X = &quot;text regtext1 text regtext2 text regtext3 text regtext4 text regtextA regtextB regtextC regtextZ end&quot;;
my ($t0,$t1,$inp,$s,$cp);

my @sampcnts = ( 5000, 7500, 10000, 15000, 20000, 25000, 30000 );
foreach my $samp (@sampcnts)
{
$inp = &quot;&quot;;

for my $cnt (1 .. $samp) {
    $inp .= $X;
}
$s = $inp;
$cp = 0;

print (&quot;\n-----------------\nSample count of lines = &quot;, $samp,  &quot;\n\n&quot; );


#########################

$t0 = new Benchmark;
while ( $inp =~ s/\G.*?\K(reg)(text\d+(?{$cp=pos()}).*?)(regtext[A-Z]+)(?{$cp+=length($^N)})/$1$3$2/sx) {
    pos($inp) = $cp;
}
$t1 = new Benchmark;
print &quot;   Regex \@sln       -took: &quot;, timestr(timediff($t1, $t0)), &quot;\n&quot;;


#############################

$t0 = new Benchmark;
while ( $s =~ /reg(text\d+).*?(regtext[A-Z]+)/g ) {
   my $ss_len = $+[2] - $-[2];   my $ss = substr( $s, $-[2], $ss_len, &quot;&quot; );
   substr( $s, $-[1], 0, $ss );
   pos( $s ) = $+[1] + $ss_len;
}
$t1 = new Benchmark;
print &quot;   Regex \@ikegami   -took: &quot;, timestr(timediff($t1, $t0)), &quot;\n\n&quot;;

if ( $inp ne $s ) 
     { print ( &quot;   Different substitution result strings\n&quot; ); }
else { print ( &quot;   Identical substitution result strings\n&quot; ); }

}
</code></pre>
