Q: Codeigniter: How to handle direct link to controller/function/param? A: <p>For a delete operation I would do a HTTP post.</p>

<pre><code>function delete()
{
    if ($id = $this-&gt;input-&gt;post('id'))
    {
        $this-&gt;item_model-&gt;delete_item($id);
    }
}
</code></pre>

<p>And then my JQuery would do a HTTP post.</p>

<pre><code>$.ajax({
    type: 'POST',
    url: 'item/delete',
    data: {id:item_id}
});
</code></pre>

<p>This way a client won't be able to accidentally delete an item through browsing to the URL in their web browser.</p>

Q: pageswap event and cross document view transition snapshots A: <p>Use pageswap/pagereveal only when names must be dynamic.</p>
<pre><code>window.addEventListener(&quot;pageswap&quot;, (e) =&gt; {
  const vt = e.viewTransition;
  if (!vt || !e.activation?.entry?.url) return;
  const to = new URL(e.activation.entry.url);

  if (to.pathname === &quot;/special/&quot;) {
    const main = document.querySelector(&quot;main&quot;);
    if (main) main.style.viewTransitionName = &quot;main&quot;;
    vt.finished.finally(() =&gt; {
      if (main) main.style.removeProperty(&quot;view-transition-name&quot;);
    });
  }
});
</code></pre>
<p>But I recommend using CSS.</p>
<pre><code>@view-transition {
  navigation: auto;
}

::view-transition-old(root),
::view-transition-new(root) {
  animation-duration: 250ms;
  animation-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1);
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  ::view-transition-old(root),
  ::view-transition-new(root) {
    animation: none;
  }
}
</code></pre>
